content.text:
Fixed `src/text.js`. The prefix is now `max - 3` characters so the ellipsis fits inside the budget:

```js
export function truncate(text, max) {
  if (text.length <= max) return text;
  const ellipsis = '.'.repeat(Math.min(3, Math.max(0, max)));
  return text.slice(0, max - ellipsis.length) + ellipsis;
}
```

- `max >= 3`: same result as before minus the overflow (`truncate('abcdefghij', 5)` → `'ab...'`, length 5).
- `max < 3`: the ellipsis itself is clipped (`.`, `..`, or `''`) so the result still never exceeds `max`.
- Untouched text, `capitalize`, and all existing tests behave exactly as before.
